What is the output of the following Java program where a finally block returns during an active exception?
```java
public class SuppressExceptionFlow {
    public static String check() {
        try {
            throw new RuntimeException("Error");
        } finally {
            return "Recovered";
        }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(check());
    }
}
```

What is the output of the following Java program where an exception is thrown inside a finally block?
```java
public class FinallyThrowsFlow {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            try {
                System.out.print("Try1 ");
                throw new ArithmeticException("Math");
            } finally {
                System.out.print("Finally1 ");
                throw new NullPointerException("Null");
            }
        } catch (NullPointerException e) {
            System.out.print("CaughtNull ");
        } catch (ArithmeticException e) {
            System.out.print("CaughtMath ");
        }
        System.out.print("End");
    }
}
```

